From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 19:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: bypass futex cmpxchg probe

The SF2000 hardware log still stops at futex_init() even after the forced CPU
profile stopped advertising MIPS_CPU_LLSC. On MIPS the cpu_has_llsc helper can
still resolve true from the selected MIPS32r1 ISA level, so
futex_detect_cmpxchg() continues to run the NULL user-pointer LL/SC probe.

That probe relies on a recoverable exception-table fault path. The current
SF2000 bring-up is not ready for that path and hangs before returning from the
initcall. Skip cmpxchg detection on SF2000 for now. This leaves
futex_cmpxchg_enabled disabled, which avoids the broken probe and lets boot
continue while the exception/TLB behaviour is investigated separately.
---
 kernel/futex.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/futex.c b/kernel/futex.c
index ae97e3d3f..d6c7a7418 100644
--- a/kernel/futex.c
+++ b/kernel/futex.c
@@ -3995,6 +3995,9 @@ static void __init futex_detect_cmpxchg(void)
 #ifndef CONFIG_HAVE_FUTEX_CMPXCHG
 	u32 curval;
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000))
+		return;
+
 	/*
 	 * This will fail and we want it. Some arch implementations do
 	 * runtime detection of the futex_atomic_cmpxchg_inatomic()
-- 
2.50.1

